G1506.d:
εἰλικρινής, -ές, 
 [in LXX: Wi 72^ kB * ;] 
unalloyed, pure (Lat. sincerus; see DCG, ii, 635a); 
  (a) of unmixed substances; 
  (b) of abstract ideas; 
  (with) of ethical purity: Phil.1:10, 2 Pet.3:1.†
 SYN.: ἁγνός (which see), καθαρός, cf. Tr., Syn.: §lxxxv; DB, iv, 176a; Cremer, 378; Westc. on 1 John.3:3. (AS)

G1519.d:
εἰς, 
 prep. with accusative,  
expressing entrance, direction, limit, into, unto, to, upon, towards, for, among (Lat. in, with accusative). 
  I. Of place. 
  1. After verbs of motion; 
  (a) of entrance into: Matt.8:23, 9:7, Mark.1:45, Luke.2:15, 8:31, al.; 
  (b) of approach, to or towards: Mark.11:1, Luke.6:8, 19:28, John.11:31, 21:6, al.; 
  (with) before pl. and collective nouns, among: Mark.4:7, 8:19, 20, Luke.11:49, John.21:23, al.; 
  (d) Of a limit reached, unto, on, upon: Matt.8:18, 21:1, Mark.11:1, 13:16, Luke.14:10, John.6:3, 11:32, al.; with accusative of person(s) (as in Ep. and Ion.), Acts.23:15, Rom.5:12, 16:19, 2 Cor.10:14; 
  (e) elliptical: ἐπιστολαὶ εἰς Δαμασκόν, Acts.9:2; ἡ διακονία μου ἡ εἰς Ἱ., Rom.15:31; metaphorically, of entrance into a certain state or condition, or of approach or direction towards some end (Thayer, B, i, 1; ii, 1), εἰς τ. ὄνομα, M, Pr., 200. 
  2. Of direction; 
  (a) after verbs of seeing: Matt.6:26, Mark.6:41, Luke.9:16, 62, John.13:22, al.; metaphorically, of the mind, Heb.11:26, 12:2, al.; 
  (b) after verbs of speaking: Matt.13:10, 14:9, 1 Thess.2:9, al.
  3. After verbs of rest; 
  (a) in "pregnant" construction, implying previous motion (cl.; see WM, 516; Bl., §39, 3; M, Pr., 234f.): Matt.2:23, 4:13, 2 Thess.2:4, 2 Tim.1:11, Heb.11:9, al.; 
  (b) by an assimilation general in late Gk (see Bl., M, Pr., ll. with) = ἐν: Luke.1:44, 4:23, Acts.20:16, 21:17, John.1:18 (but see Westc, in l.), al. 
  II. Of time, for, unto; 
  1. accentuating the duration expressed by the accusative: εἰς τ. αἰῶνα, Matt.21:19; εἰς γενεὰς καὶ γ., Luke.1:50; εἰς τ. διηνεκές, Heb.7:3, al. 
  2. Of a point or limit of time, unto, up to, until: Matt.6:34, Acts.4:3, 25:21, Phil.1:10, 2:16, 1 Thess.4:15, 2 Tim.1:12; of entrance into a future period, σεις τὸ μέλλον (see: μέλλω), next (year), Luke.13:9 (but with ICC, in l.); εἰς τ. μεταξὺ σάββατον, on the next Sabbath, Acts.13:42; εἰς τὸ πάλιν (see: πάλιν, 2 Cor.13:2. 
  III. Of result, after verbs of changing, joining, dividing, etc.: στρέφειν εἰς, Rev.11:6; μετας-, Acts.2:20, Jas.4:9; μεταλλάσσειν, Rom.1:26; σχίζειν εἰς δύο, Matt.27:51, al.; predicatively with εἴναι, Acts.8:23. 
  IV. Of relation, to, towards, for, in regard to (so in cl., but more frequently in late Gk., εἰς encroaching on the simple dative, which it has wholly displaced in MGr.; Jannaris, Gr., §1541; Robertson, Gr., 594; Deiss., BS, 117f.): Luke.7:30, Rom.4:20, 15:2, 26, 1 Cor.16:1, Eph.3:16, al.; ἀγάπη εἰς, Rom.5:8, al.; χρηστός, Eph.4:32; φρονεῖν εἰς, Rom.12:16; θαρρεῖν, 2 Cor.10:1. 
  V. Of the end or object: εὔθετος εἰς, Luke.14:34; σόφος, Rom.16:19; ἰσχύειν, Matt.5:13; εἰς τοῦτο, Mark.1:38, al.; ἀφορίζειν εἰς, Rom.1:1; indicating purpose, εἰς φόβον, Rom.8:15; εἰς ἔνδειξιν, Rom.3:25; εἰς τό, with inf. (= ἵνα or ὥστε; Bl., §71, 5; M, Pr., 218ff.): Matt.20:19, Rom.1:11, 1 Cor.9:18, al. 
  VI. Adverbial phrases: εἰς τέλος, εἰς τὸ πάλιν, etc (see: τέλος, πάλιν, etc.).
 (AS)

G1520.d:
εἷς 
 ιά, ἕν, genitive ἑνός, μιᾶς, ἑνός, 
 cardinal numeral, one; 
  1. one, as opposite to many: Matt.25:15, Rom.5:12, 1 Cor.10:8, al.; as subst., Rom.5:15, Eph.2:14; id. with genitive partit., Matt.5:19, al.; before ἐκ (ἐξ), Mark.14:18, John.6:8, al.; metaphorically, of union and concord, John.10:30 17:11, Rom.12:4-5, Phil.1:27; ἀπὸ μιᾶς (B1., § 44, 1), Luke.14:18; with neg., εἷς. . . οὐ (μή), more emphatic than οὐδείς, no one, none (cl.), Matt.5:18 10:29, Luke.11:46 12:6. 
  2. Emphatically, to the exclusion of others; 
  (a) a single (one): Matt.21:24, Mark.8:14; absol., 1 Cor.9:24, al.; οὐδὲ εἷς, Matt.27:14, John.1:3, Rom.3:10, al.; 
  (b) one, alone: Mark.2:7 10:18, Luke.18:19; 
  (with) one and the same: Rom.3:30, 1 Cor.3:8 11:5 12:11, 1 John.5:8. 
  3. In late Gk., with weakened force, = τις or indef. art. (of. Heb. אֶחָד, Gen.22:13, al.; see B1., § 45, 2; M, Pr., 96 f.): Matt.8:19 19:6, Rev.8:13, al.; εἷς τις (Bl., l.with), Luke.22:50, John.11:49 
  4. Distributively: εἷς καστος (cl.), Luke.4:40, Acts.2:6, al.; εἷς . . . καὶ εἷς (cl., εἷς μὲν . . . εἷς δέ), Matt.17:4, Mark.9:5, John.20:12, al. (cf. LXX and use of Heb. אֶחָד, Exod.17:12, al); ὁ εἷς . . . ὁ ἕτερος (ἄλλος) = cl. ὁ μὲν (ἕτερος) . . . ὁ δέ (ἕτερος), Matt.6:24, Luke.7:41, Rev.17:10; καθ᾽ εἷς, εἷς κ. είς (in which καθ᾽ is adverbial, or the expression formed from the analogy of ἕν καθ᾽ ἔν; M, Pr., 105), one by one, severally: Mark.14:19, Rom.12:5, al.; εἷς τὸν ἕνα = ἀλλήλους (B1., 45, 2; M, Pr., 246), 1 Thess.5:11. 
  5. As ordinal = πρῶτος (like Heb. אֶחָד; Bl., § 45, 1; M, Pr., 95 f.), first: Matt.28:1, Mark.16:2, al 
 (AS)

G1577.d:
ἐκκλησία, -ας, ἡ 
 (ἐκ-καλέω), [in LXX chiefly for קָהָל, otherwise for one of its cogn. forms ;] 
  1. prop., an assembly of citizens regularly convened (in Thuc., ii, 22, opposite to σύλλογος, a concourse): Acts.19:32, 39 41. 
  2. In LXX of the assembly, congregation, community of Israel (Deu.4:10 23:2, al.): Acts.7:38, Heb.2:12" (LXX) . 
  3. NT, esp. of an assembly or company of Christians, a (the) church; 
  (a) of gatherings for worship:  1 Cor.11:18 14:19, 34 35; 
  (b) of local communities: Acts.8:3, 1 Cor.4:17; with name added, Acts.8:1, Rom.16:1, 1 Thess.1:1, al.; pl., Acts.15:41, 1 Cor.7:17; τ. Χριστοῦ, Rom.16:16; τ. Ἀσίας, 1 Cor.16:19; τ. ἁγίων, 1 Cor.14:33; εἰπο]ν τ. ἐκκλησίᾳ, Matt.18:17 (but see Hort, Ecclesia, 10); of a house-congregation (DB, i, 431a), Rom.16:5, 1 Cor.16:19, Col.4:15, Phm 2; 
  (with) of the whole body of Christians: Matt.16:18, 1 Cor.12:28, Eph.1:22, Phil.3:6, al.; τ. θεοῦ, Acts.20:28 (Κυρίου, T, R, mg.), 1 Cor.15:9, Gal.1:13, 1 Tim.3:15; ἐ. προτοτόκων ἀπογεγραμμένων ἐν οὐρανοῖς, Heb.12:23. 
 SYN.: συναγωγή, which see (see Tr., Syn., §i; DB, i, 426; Hort, Ecclesia, esp. 4ff., 107ff.; Hamilton, People of God, ii, 37ff.; reff. s.vv. "Church," "Congregation," in DB and DCG; Cremer, 332). (AS)

G1588.d:
ἐκ-λεκτός, -ή, -όν 
 (ἐκλέγω), [in LXX for בָּחַר (so prob. in Isa.28:16, Pro.17:3, for MT בָּחַן), בָּרִיא, etc. ;] 
  1. choice, select (cl., rarely; Thuc., Plat., al.), hence, eminent: Rom.16:13 (cf. Eze.27:24). 
  2. As in  Inscr. (MM, Exp., xii), chosen; esp. as in LXX, of Israel, elect, chosen of God (Isa.65:9, Ps.105:43, al.); so in NT; 
  (a) of Christ: Luke.23:35 (cf. Isa.42:1); figuratively, λίθος, 1 Pet.2:4-6 (LXX); 
  (b) of holy angels: 1 Tim.5:21; 
  (with) of Christians: Matt.24:22, 24, Mark.13:20, 22 13:27, 2 Tim.2:10, 1 Pet.1:1; τ. θεοῦ, Luke.18:7, Rom.8:33, Col.3:12, Titus.1:1; τ. Χριστοῦ, Matt.24:31; ἐ. κυρία, II Jn 1; ἀδελφή, II Jn 13; γένος, 1 Pet.2:9 (LXX); κλητοὶ καὶ ἐ. κ. πιστοί, Rev.17:14; opposite to κλητός (not so in Epp.; see Lft. on Col.3:12), Matt.20:16 (T, WH, txt., R, omit) Matt.22:14 (Cremer, 405, 775).†
 (AS)

G1658.d:
ἐλεύθερος, -α, -ον 
 [in LXX chiefly for חׇפְשִׁי ;] 
free; 
  (a) in civil sense, not a slave: John.8:33, 1 Cor.7:21-22 12:13, Gal.3:28, Eph.6:8, Col.3:11, Rev.6:15 13:16 19:18; fem., Gal.4:22-23, 30; 
  (b) as regards restraint and obligation in general: Matt.17:26, 1 Cor.9:1; before ἐκ, 1 Cor.9:19; ἀπό, Rom.7:3; with inf., 1 Cor.7:39; from the law, Gal.4:26, 1 Pet.2:16;  from sin, John.8:32, 36; τῇ δικαιοσύνῃ, as regards righteousness, Rom.6:20 (Cremer, 249).†
 (AS)

G1715.d:
ἔμ-προσθεν 
 adv. 
of place (in cl. also of time), 
 [in LXX chiefly for עֳנִי ;] 
  1. adverbially, before, in front: Luke.19:28; εἰς τὸ ἔ., Luke.19:4; opposite to ὄπισθεν, Rev.4:6; opposite to τὰ ὀπίσω, τὰ ἔ., Phil.3:13. 
  2. As prep., before; 
  (a) in front of: Matt.5:24 6:2 7:6 11:10 27:29, Luke.5:19 7:27 14:2, John.3:28 10:4, Rev.19:10 22:8; 
  (b) in the presence of: Matt.27:11, Gal.2:14, 1 Thess.1:3 2:19 3:9 3:13; ὁμολουεῖν, ἀρνεῖσθαι (Dalman, Words, 210), Matt.10:32, 36 26:70, Luke.12:8; in forensic sense, Matt.25:32 27:11, Luke.21:36, Acts.18:17, 2 Cor.5:10, 1 Thess.2:19, I Jn  3:19; εὐδοκία (θέλημά) ἐστι ἔ. θεοῦ (a targumic formula; Dalman, Words, 211), Matt.11:26 18:14, Luke.10:21; 
  (with) in the sight of: Matt.5:16 6:1 17:2 23:14, Mark.2:12 9:2, Luke.19:27, John.12:37, Acts.10:4; 
  (d) of rank and dignity (Dem., Plat., al.; LXX, Gen.48:20): John.1:15, 30.†
 (AS)

G1764.d:
ἐν-ίστημι 
 [in LXX: 4Ki.13:6 A (עֶמְדָּה), 3Ki.12:24, 1Es.5:47 Est.9:6, Est.3:13, 1; 4Ma.9.1-32 * ;] 
to place in; in pf., plpf., 2 aor. and in mid., intrans.; 
  (a) to be at hand, impend, threaten: 2 Tim.3:1; 
  (b) to be present: 2 Thess.2:2 (but see Thayer, see word); pf. ptcp., present: 1 Cor.7:26, Gal.1:4, Heb.9:9; pl., Rom.8:38, 1 Cor.3:22 (Cremer, 3O9).†
 (AS)

G1785.d:
ἐντολή, -ῆς, ἡ
 (ἐντέλλω, which see), [in LXX chiefly for מִצְוָה; in pl. frequently in Pss for פִּקּוּד ;] 
  1. generally, a charge, injunction, order, command: Luke.15:29, John.10:18 11:57 12:49-50 14:31, Acts.17:15, Col.4:10; ἐ. σαρκίνη, Heb.7:16, 18 
  2. Esp. of religious precepts and commandments; 
  (a) of God's commandments: in OT, Matt.15:3 22:36, 38 22:40 Mk  7:8-9; Mark.10:5, 19 12:28, 31 Eph.2:15, Heb.9:19; esp. of the decalogue, Matt.5:19 19:17, Mark.10:19, Luke.18:20 23:56, Rom.7:8-13 13:9, Eph.6:2; of God's command­ments in general, Luke.1:6, 1 Cor.7:19, 1 John.2:3-8 Jn 3:22-24 Jn 4:21 Jn 5:2-3, Rev.12:17 14:12; collectively, ἡ ἐ. (cf. τ. ἔργον τ. θεοῦ, John.6:29), 1 Tim.6:14, 2 Pet.2:21 3:2; 
  (b) of things commanded Christ by the Father: John.12:49-50 14:31 15:10; 
  (with) of the precepts of Christ: John.13:34 14:15, 21 15:10, 12, 1 Cor.14:37. 
  3. Phrases: before ἵνα, John.13:34 15:12, 1 John.3:23 Jn 4:21, 2 John.6; ἐντολὴν (ὰς) παραβαίνειν, Matt.15:3; ἀκυροῦν, Matt.15:6 Rec.; τηρεῖν, Matt.19:17 John.15:10, al.; ποιεῖν, 1 John.5:2; διδόναι, John.11:57; λαμβάνειν, John.10:18, 2 John.4; ἔχειν, John.14:21, Heb.7:5; ἐ. καὶ δικαιώματα, Luke.1:6; ἐντολαὶ ἀνθρώπων (of Jewish tradition), Titus.1:14; i. καινή, John.13:34, 1 John.2:7, 2 John.5.†
 (AS)

G1854.d:
ἔξω 
 adv. (ἐξ), [in LXX for חוּץ ;] 
  1. outside, without; 
  (a) adverbially: Matt.12:46, Mark.3:31 11:4, Luke.8:20, John.18:16, al.; with art., ὁ ἔ., he who is without; metaphorically, in pl., οἱ ἔ., of those outside the Church, 1 Cor.5:12-13, Col.4:5 (Lft., in l), 1 Thess.4:12; ὁ ἔ. ἄνθρωπος, 2 Cor.4:16; αἱ ἔ. πόλεις, Acts.26:11; 
  (b) as prep. with genitive: Luke.13:33, Acts.21:5, Heb.13:11-12 
  2. After verbs of motion; 
  (a) adverbially, forth, out: Matt.5:13 Mark.14:68, Luke.22:62, John.19:4, 13, Acts.9:40, al.; 
  (b) as prep. with genitive, out of: Matt.21:17, Mark.11:19 12:8, Luke.4:29, Acts.7:58, Heb.13:13, al 
 (AS)

G1861.d:
ἐπ-αγγέλλω 
 [in LXX: Est.4:8 (אָמַר), Pro.13:12, Wis.2:13, al. ;] 
  1. to announce, proclaim. 
  2. (a) to promise; 
  (b) to profess. Mid., also frequently in both these senses; 
  (with) to promise: with dab. of person(s), Heb.6:13; with accusative of thing(s), Rom.4:21, Titus.1:2; with dative of person(s) and accusative of thing(s), Jas.1:12 2:5, 2 Pet.2:19; ἐπαγγελίαν, 1 John.2:25; with inf., Mark.14:11, Acts.7:5; before λέγων, Heb.12:26; ptcp., Heb.10:23 11:11; 
  (d) to profess: θεοσέβειαν, 1 Tim.2:10; γνῶσιν, 1 Tim.6:21. Pass., Gal.3:19 (cf. προ-επαγγέλλω; and see Cremer, 26).†
 (AS)

G1883.d:
ἐπ-άνω 
 adv., [in LXX for מַעֲלָה, עַל, מֵעָל, etc. ;] 
above; 
  1. adverbially; 
  (a) of place: Luke.11:44; 
  (b) of number, more than: Mark.14:5, 1 Cor.15:6. 
  2. As prep. C. genitive; 
  (a) of place: Matt.2:9 5:14 21:7 23:18-22 27:37 28:2, Luke.4:39 10:19, Rev.6:8 20:3; 
  (b) of pre-eminence: Luke.19:17-19, John.3:31.†
 (AS)

G1921.d:
ἐπι-γινώσκω 
 [in LXX chiefly for נָכַר: hi., also for יָדַע, etc. ;] 
"directive" of γινώσκω (AR, Eph., 249), as in cl.; 
  1. to observe, perceive, discern, recognize; 
  (a) absol.: Acts.25:10, 1 Cor.13:12; before ὅτι, Luke.1:22; τ. πνεύματι, before ὅτι, Mark.2:8; 
  (b) with accusative of thing(s): Luke.1:4 5:22, Acts.12:14 27:39, Rom.1:32, 2 Cor.1:13, Col.1:6, 1 Tim.4:3; ἐν ἐαυτῷ, Mark.5:30; before ὅτι, 1 Cor.14:37; 
  (with) with accusative of person(s): Matt.11:27 14:36 17:12, Mark.6:33 (T, αὐτούς, but LTr., WH, R, omit the prop., and LTr., WH, txt., read ἔγνωσαν), Mark.6:54 Luke.24:16, 31, 1 Cor.16:18, 2 Cor.1:14; before ἀπό, with genitive of thing(s), Matt.7:16, 20; before ὅτι, Acts.3:10 4:13, 2 Cor.13:5; pass., 1 Cor.13:12; opposite to ἀγνοούμενοι, 2 Cor.6:9. 
  2. to discover, ascertain, determine: Acts.9:30; before ὅτι, Luke.7:37 23:7, Acts.19:34 22:29 24:11 28:1; with accusative of thing(s), before quæst., Acts.23:28; δι᾽ ἣν αἰτίαν, Acts.22:24; παρά, with genitive of person(s), before περ, with genitive of thing(s), Acts.24:8; τ. ὁδὸν τῆς δικαιοσύνης, 2 Pet.2:21 (cf. Lft., Col., 136; Cremer, 159; M, Pr., 113; AR, Eph., 248 ff.).†
 (AS)
